<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Zend collects, uses and protects your information.">
  <p class="pg-updated">Last updated: 14 November 2026</p>

  <p>
    Zend helps people buy and sell on social media without fear. To do that, we need to look after your information carefully. This page explains, in plain words, what we collect, why, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Zend is a new company being set up in Nigeria by the Zend team, and it isn't registered yet. Until it is, the Zend team is responsible for your information. When this policy says "Zend", "we" or "us", it means us. If you have any question about your information, write to us at <a href="mailto:officialzendit@gmail.com">officialzendit@gmail.com</a> or use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect right now</h2>
  <p>Zend hasn't launched yet. Today, the only information we collect is what you give us yourself. When you join the waitlist, that's:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name</li>
    <li>your phone number or your email address</li>
    <li>the date and time you joined, and which button you used to join</li>
  </ul>
  <p>When you send us a message through our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, we receive your name, your email address and your message, so we can reply.</p>
  <p>We don't ask for your bank details, card details or passwords, and we never will through this website.</p>

  <h2>What we use it for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To tell you when Zend is ready for you to use.</li>
    <li>To send you a few updates about Zend before launch. You can ask us to stop at any time.</li>
    <li>To count how many people have joined (for example, the number shown on our home page). That count shows no names or contact details.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell your information, and we don't share it with advertisers.</p>

  <h2>Where it's kept</h2>
  <p>
    Waitlist sign-ups and contact messages are stored in a private Google Sheet that only the Zend team can open, and contact messages also arrive in our Gmail inbox. Google stores this data for us under its own security and privacy terms. We only keep your information for as long as we need it for the reasons above, or until you ask us to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>When Zend launches</h2>
  <p>
    Once you start buying and selling with Zend, we'll need more information to process payments safely: for example, details of your orders and payments. Payments are recorded on the Stellar network. We'll update this policy before launch and tell you about the changes before we collect anything new.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us at any time to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>show you the information we hold about you</li>
    <li>correct it if it's wrong</li>
    <li>delete it, which also removes you from the waitlist</li>
    <li>stop sending you updates</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Just write to <a href="mailto:officialzendit@gmail.com">officialzendit@gmail.com</a> or use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, and mention the phone number or email you signed up with. If you're not happy with how we've handled your information, you can also complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and storage on your device</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages are useful. It sets cookies and tells us things like how many people visited and which pages they viewed, but not who you are. We don't use advertising cookies. The website also saves a few small things on your device so it works smoothly:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>whether you prefer day or night mode</li>
    <li>where you were on the page, so a reload brings you back to the same spot</li>
    <li>a copy of the website's files, so it loads faster next time and still opens without a connection</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Those three stay on your device. You can clear them, and the analytics cookies, any time from your browser's settings.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Zend is only for people who are old enough, where they live, to buy and sell and to make agreements on their own (in Nigeria, that's 18). We don't knowingly collect information from anyone younger. If you think someone under that age has joined the waitlist, tell us and we'll delete it.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we'll update the date at the top of this page. If the change is important, we'll also tell people on the waitlist.</p>
</PageLayout>
